                       "description":  "Before starting a recording, users can configure capture settings through a collapsible settings panel. The primary setting is video FPS, which controls the frame rate of screen recording and can be adjusted between 10 and 60 FPS using a slider. Higher FPS produces smoother video but larger files, with 30 FPS recommended as the default. Settings are disabled during an active recording to prevent mid-session configuration changes that could corrupt data.",
